<p>It&#8217;s a <a href="https://www.relay.fm/mpu/851">feedback episode</a>, which means Stephen and I finally crack open the mailbag that&#8217;s been piling up. I went hard at Apple Home since we last talked. I nuked my twelve-year-old setup, ran Ethernet cable around the house for Aqara cameras, and put in an Aqara U400 lock that opens when I walk up with my arms full of groceries. </p>



<p>We also get into the smart scale I&#8217;m sending back, why I still process raw photos in Pixelmator Pro, and the risk-and-reward math of letting an AI read your email. Stephen brought actual contraband to this one, a DJI Osmo Pocket 4 that &#8220;fell off a truck&#8221; in front of his house. I talk about my new TRMNL X e-ink display, the new MCP server DEVONthink 4.3 added, and my long-running campaign to get Stephen to back up off-site. </p>



<p>Over in More Power Users, Stephen walks through every piece of gear he&#8217;s hauling to WWDC. Come for the home automation, stay for the battery hoarding.</p>



